From c02678e33cd96f6d117811c46a2bb9a0c88fe91e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 14:00:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10787/11362] [outer-loop] Refit the VRAM envelope to the
 Qwen3.8-27B pin (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6880)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The predictor still used the gemma-4-31B envelope for the current pin,
over-predicting -c 98304 by ~4.4 GB. That forced an 11-layer FFN offload
(decode 28 -> 13.1 tok/s, ~8 under conductor contention), which pushed
think-mode induces past the 2400s timeout -- measured directly: a real
r11l induce at 98304 generated 19.2k/18.5k tokens per attempt, truncated=0
(pool fix HELD), and timed out with chars_final=0.

Nine per-PID residencies measured 2026-09-02 (q8 KV, RTX 3090): slope
0.0403 MiB/cell (4-slot same-layer segment), intercept 15768 anchored
through the worst 4-slot residual so every guard-shape point is
over-predicted (max +223) and nothing is under-predicted by more than
377 (margin 1500). Per-layer credit is a bounded 150 estimate: launch
scatter (~±150) swamps it -- a 0-layer launch measured below a 1-layer
one. Gemma constants kept as the historical record per never-prune.

Consequences, verified: at 98304 the auto-fit picks 0 layers (was 11)
and at the default 106496 a free 3090 admits without offload (measured
footprint 20664 vs guard 22387) -- retiring the 'single-stream dev
harnesses must override' workaround's root cause. Three tests re-anchored
from gemma measured footprints to the Qwen direct measurements, each with
the retarget reasoning in place; new envelope test pins all nine points.

Mutation-proven: reverting the predictor to the gemma constants turns 2
of 3 new envelope tests RED; restored byte-identical (cmp), 25/25 green.

Mutation-gate marker 48f0652489ac deleted deliberately: it paired MY
envelope-test run with a concurrent agent's research-references.md edit,
tagged NOT-this-run and never observed being written by the tests. That
file is untouched by this commit and left in the tree for its author.

